  "id": "RAW_77b634f808",
  "title": "你的 AI 在正常网络上发现了故障",
  "url": "https://theainetworkengineer.substack.com/p/your-ai-found-a-fault-on-a-healthy",
  "date": "2026-11-27 23:06:33",
  "author": "Infra Engg Hub By Packt",
  "siteName": "The AI Network Engineer",
  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <div class=\"post-header\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Post header\">\n   <h3 class=\"subtitle subtitle-HEEcLo\" dir=\"auto\">A vague ticket can make an agent search until something looks guilty</h3>\n   <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-paddingBottom-16 pc-reset\" aria-label=\"Post UFI\" role=\"region\">\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-paddingY-16 pc-justifyContent-space-between pc-alignItems-center pc-reset\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-12 pc-alignItems-center pc-reset byline-wrapper\">\n      <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-reset\">\n       <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-4 pc-reset\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-reset color-secondary-Y_KLZk line-height-20-DxeVem font-meta-mBdcth size-11-Pn75Jw weight-medium-W9KlJB transform-uppercase-m8PhL1 reset-KrJVVF meta-jfcJ27\">\n         <time datetime=\"2026-11-27T15:06:33.157Z\" title=\"2026-11-27T15:06:33.157Z\">Nov 27, 2026</time>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-16 pc-justifyContent-space-between pc-alignItems-center pc-reset flex-grow-zFd_bz post-ufi\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n      <div class=\"like-button-container post-ufi-button style-button\">\n       <button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft post-ufi-button style-button no-label with-border\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Like\" aria-pressed=\"false\"></button>\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft post-ufi-button style-button post-ufi-comment-button no-label with-border\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"View comments (0)\" data-href=\"https://theainetworkengineer.substack.com/p/your-ai-found-a-fault-on-a-healthy/comments\"></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft post-ufi-button style-button no-label with-border\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-haspopup=\"menu\" id=\"base-ui-_R_ecv328smd5alip_\"></button>\n     </div>\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n      <button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft post-ufi-button style-button has-label with-border\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"> \n       <div class=\"label\">Share</div> \n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n   <div class=\"dt-post-body\">\n    <div class=\"available-content\">\n     <div class=\"body markup\" dir=\"auto\">\n      <h2 class=\"header-anchor-post\">Your AI Troubleshooter Needs a “No Fault Observed” Exit\n       <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n         <button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-ygWCr5 iconButtonBase-JffdAc buttonBase-tqxFUX buttonStyle-mAh5l3 size_sm-Ohhhwq priority_secondary-AkqbVJ\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" data-href=\"https://theainetworkengineer.substack.com/i/226786030/your-ai-troubleshooter-needs-a-no-fault-observed-exit\"> \n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n           <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n          </svg> \n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div></h2>\n      <p>A ticket comes in saying the gateway keeps flapping, so your AI troubleshooter checks the interface state, adjacency history and reachability. Everything looks stable during the reported window.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">What should it do next?</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">The useful answer is a scoped one: no gateway flap was observed using the available evidence during that window. But an agent built to find root causes can find that answer strangely difficult. Instead of stopping, it may continue probing until an old route, an unrelated warning or a harmless configuration difference starts to look like the RCA.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span>That’s the failure mode examined in </span><strong><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27021\">FaulT-Bench</a></strong><span>, a recent preprint testing three troubleshooting agents against accurate, misleading and false-premise network tickets.</span></p>\n      <h3 class=\"header-anchor-post\">A ticket is a claim, not a fact\n       <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n         <button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-ygWCr5 iconButtonBase-JffdAc buttonBase-tqxFUX buttonStyle-mAh5l3 size_sm-Ohhhwq priority_secondary-AkqbVJ\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" data-href=\"https://theainetworkengineer.substack.com/i/226786030/a-ticket-is-a-claim-not-a-fact\"> \n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n           <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n          </svg> \n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div></h3>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">The agents performed well when a genuine fault was described accurately. The harder case was a ticket reporting a fault on a healthy network.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">On the standard false-premise tickets, the three agents reported a fault in 11% to 24% of the runs that produced an answer. They often disproved the reported symptom correctly, but then continued investigating until a genuine yet benign condition could be presented as the cause.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">The wording of the ticket made a surprising difference.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">A non-technical ticket that confidently blamed a specific component behaved much like a standard technical ticket. Even though the claim was wrong, the agent had something concrete to test.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">A vague ticket was harder. When the ticket provided no clear cause, the average outcome score fell from 0.820 to 0.675. Remove the verifiable identifiers as well, and pooled overdiagnosis across the three agents reached 47%.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">In other words, the biggest problem wasn’t a confident user pointing the agent in the wrong direction. The agents could test a specific claim and reject it. The trouble started when the ticket gave them nothing precise to disprove.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">There was another uncomfortable result. The skills-augmented agent produced the best-grounded investigation traces, yet it also overdiagnosed most often on the standard healthy-network cases. The same extra diagnostic capability that helped it localize genuine faults gave it more benign conditions to point at when no fault existed.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">More tools don’t automatically make an agent more trustworthy if it still lacks a criterion for concluding, with evidence, that no fault was observed.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">There are limits to what we should take from the numbers. FaulT-Bench is a preprint based on emulated networks, authored tickets, three agents and an LLM judge. These aren’t production failure rates. What the study gives us is a useful failure mode to test for in our own workflows.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">It also connects neatly to the interface-flap issue we covered last week. There, the problem was that sampled metrics could miss a transition between two green data points, so the investigation needed transition logs covering the incident window.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">This is the other side of that problem. If the metrics, transition logs, adjacency history and reachability checks cover the reported window and show no flap, the agent needs to accept that result. It shouldn’t keep searching until something else looks suspicious.</p>\n      <h3 style=\"text-align:justify\" class=\"header-anchor-post\">Give “no fault observed” a valid exit\n       <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n         <button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-ygWCr5 iconButtonBase-JffdAc buttonBase-tqxFUX buttonStyle-mAh5l3 size_sm-Ohhhwq priority_secondary-AkqbVJ\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" data-href=\"https://theainetworkengineer.substack.com/i/226786030/give-no-fault-observed-a-valid-exit\"> \n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n           <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n          </svg> \n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div></h3>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">You already accept this outcome from Ansible.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span>A play can finish with </span><code>ok=5</code><span> </span><code>changed=0</code><span> </span><code>failed=0</code><span>, and that’s a successful run. The playbook completed, the checks passed and nothing needed changing.</span></p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">An RCA workflow needs the same legitimate outcome. It shouldn’t be forced to choose between finding a fault and failing to complete.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">I’d give it three terminal states:</p>\n      <blockquote>\n       <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-8 pc-padding-20 pc-reset bg-primary-pC6prJ outline-detail-MZomZU pc-borderRadius-sm sizing-border-box-tYLTRQ container-KfNFl_\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-reset overflow-auto-qlSiR4 scrollBar-hidden-_AZ9yg code-G_k53t\" data-line-numbers=\"true\">\n         <pre><code>fault_confirmed\nno_fault_observed\ninsufficient_evidence</code></pre>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </blockquote>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">These state names and the contract below are our suggested implementation, not something provided by the paper.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><code>fault_confirmed</code><span> means the reported symptom was reproduced and supported by the required evidence.</span></p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><code>no_fault_observed</code><span> means the agent completed the defined checks across a specified scope and time window without observing the reported condition.</span></p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><code>insufficient_evidence</code><span> means the agent couldn’t complete those checks or the available evidence didn’t cover the claim.</span></p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">Here’s a small contract you can adapt:</p>\n      <blockquote>\n       <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-8 pc-padding-20 pc-reset bg-primary-pC6prJ outline-detail-MZomZU pc-borderRadius-sm sizing-border-box-tYLTRQ container-KfNFl_\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-reset overflow-auto-qlSiR4 scrollBar-hidden-_AZ9yg code-G_k53t\" data-line-numbers=\"true\">\n         <pre><code>Investigation result: \n- fault_confirmed \n- no_fault_observed \n- insufficient_evidence \n\nTo return no_fault_observed, record: \n- the reported symptom \n- the investigation window \n- the devices and interfaces checked \n- the commands, parameters and vantage points used \n- the evidence that contradicted the report \n- any part of the claim that could not be verified \n\nDo not continue searching for another cause unless a new, independent signal indicates a fault. \n\nDo not promote an unrelated warning, historical event or benign configuration difference into the root cause.</code></pre>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </blockquote>\n      <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n       <figure>\n        <a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"> \n         <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n          <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:724,&quot;width&quot;:1384,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:82668,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://theainetworkengineer.substack.com/i/226786030?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181045_00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_00596c26-5038-4476-9755-33139e26fa25_1384x724.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture>\n          <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n           <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n            <button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-tqxFUX\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-tqxFUX\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"> \n             <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\">\n              <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n             </svg> \n            </button>\n           </div>\n          </div>\n         </div> \n        </a>\n        <figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Finding no evidence of the reported fault is a valid result. Failing to collect enough evidence is a different result.</figcaption>\n       </figure>\n      </div>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">For the gateway ticket, the final answer could look like this:</p>\n      <blockquote>\n       <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-8 pc-padding-20 pc-reset bg-primary-pC6prJ outline-detail-MZomZU pc-borderRadius-sm sizing-border-box-tYLTRQ container-KfNFl_\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-reset overflow-auto-qlSiR4 scrollBar-hidden-_AZ9yg code-G_k53t\" data-line-numbers=\"true\">\n         <pre><code>Verdict: no_fault_observed\n\nNo gateway flap was observed between 10:00 and 10:30 UTC.\n\nInterface-transition logs, adjacency history and reachability\nchecks remained stable for the named gateway during that window.\n\nThis result applies only to the devices, signals and time window\nlisted above.</code></pre>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </blockquote>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">That’s more useful than “nothing is wrong with the network,” which claims far more than the checks established. It’s also better than an RCA built around the first unrelated anomaly the agent happened to find.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">A capable troubleshooter doesn’t need to produce a root cause every time. Sometimes the right outcome is to show what it checked, define the limits of that evidence and stop.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">Does your troubleshooting workflow have a legitimate way to return “no fault observed,” or does every investigation have to find something guilty? Hit reply and tell me.</p>\n      <h4 class=\"header-anchor-post\">Before we wrap up, make AI Infrastructure Engineering Part of your learning journey\n       <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n         <button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-ygWCr5 iconButtonBase-JffdAc buttonBase-tqxFUX buttonStyle-mAh5l3 size_sm-Ohhhwq priority_secondary-AkqbVJ\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" data-href=\"https://theainetworkengineer.substack.com/i/226786030/before-we-wrap-up-make-ai-infrastructure-engineering-part-of-your-learning-journey\"> \n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n           <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n          </svg> \n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div></h4>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\">Through this newsletter, we always strive to help you not only understand what’s changing in our industry but also develop the skills to work with those changes.</p>\n      <p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span>Our </span><strong><a href=\"https://luma.com/ai-infra-engg\">AI Infrastructure Engineering Membership Pass</a></strong><span> is designed to help you build those skills through expert-led, hands-on workshops focused on real-world engineering challenges.</span></p>\n      <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n       <figure>\n        <a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://luma.com/ai-infra-engg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"> \n         <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n          <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_3d121305-987b-4e21-8e0d-212d44eeb470_900x256.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261127181046_3d121305-987b-4e21-8e0d-212d44eeb470_900x256.png 848w, https://media.b